# Pyodide does not only READ packageCacheDir, it WRITES to it: every wheel it fetches during a
# run is cached here (cryptography, cffi, openssl-*.zip and friends — several MB). Only the two
# wheels this repository deliberately vendors are tracked, so a local gate run cannot leave
# megabytes of downloaded wheels staged for commit.
*
!.gitignore
!micropip-0.6.0-py3-none-any.whl
!packaging-23.2-py3-none-any.whl
